(Bug #72's guard: a map copied into a second name is one heap object under
 two names, and a `Set` through either puts the key in. The proof is
 withheld for both ends of the copy, so #54's rejection still stands.)

a map called guess is {"a": "t"}.
a map called other is guess.
Set other's "absent" to "here".
a number called n is guess's "absent".
Print n.
